{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Esau ran.</b> His heart was transformed in an instant through Jacob's humility, as is the way with the descendants of Esau in exile — who, in his arrogance, says: מִי יוֹרִידֵנוּ אָרֶץ. And it was shown that we are saved from the sword of his pride through humility and gift-offering, as the Sages, of blessed memory, stated (Ta'anit 20b): that Ahijah the Shilonite prophesied against Israel with a reed that bends to every wind (I Kings 14:15). Had they done so in the battles of the Second Temple, our Temple would not have been destroyed, as Rabbi Yohanan ben Zakkai testified, saying (Gittin 56a): בִּרְיוֹנֵי דְבָן לָא שָׁבְקִינָן."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The phrase מִי יוֹרִידֵנוּ אָרֶץ appears to be a citation of Obadiah 1:3 or similar; kept in Hebrew as Sforno quotes it. The Aramaic phrase בִּרְיוֹנֵי דְבָן לָא שָׁבְקִינָן from Gittin 56a is left in Hebrew script per instructions; it means 'the battles of Ben-', a truncated form of the original Aramaic referring to internal strife."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:13.060921624Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}